:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/rburing","id":229837,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTgzNw==","login":"rburing","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing"},"body":"In some parts of the engine like soft bodies and joints it seems hard to make progress without breaking compatibility and/or ignoring current GodotPhysics3D behavior (unless someone wants to sponsor work on GodotPhysics3D, or adding extra compatibility code/settings, which I highly doubt). As you wrote we can document it in the upgrade guide as a behavior change (and document the difference between engines in the class reference, as already done in the PR). It should also be highlighted in the blog post of the first dev build that includes the change.\n\nI'm in favor of adding this missing feature and breaking compat.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114198#pullrequestreview-3802670243","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114198","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-02-14T21:19:44Z"}]